From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:18:50 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] Plutonium: the server's thread environment, auth and
 network access

Folded from:
- list agent-launched native windows under their thread
- apps in the right panel, terminal tagging, pop out
- use the Plutonium helper and its agent bridge
- what the user starts comes to the front; a toast for the rest
- network access from the shell's settings
- agents drive windows and tabs
- auth session issue --runtime-mode-ceiling, for MCP clients that launch threads
- an archived or deleted thread's permission grants are forgotten
- remote clients see native windows
- native windows are their threads' server tabs
